WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.607
Scenario: Two hosts are isolated after a suspected platform compromise,

2
00:00:05.607 --> 00:00:11.215
but data-access scope and recovery time remain unknown. Safest response:

3
00:00:11.215 --> 00:00:16.822
brief the board on verified facts, impacts, containment, uncertainties, owners

4
00:00:16.822 --> 00:00:22.430
and the next update. Option A is unsafe because No

5
00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:28.037
confirmed exfiltration does not prove that data was not accessed.

6
00:00:28.037 --> 00:00:33.645
Option B is unsafe because Leadership needs timely decision-ready information

7
00:00:33.645 --> 00:00:39.252
before attribution is complete. Option D is unsafe because Raw

8
00:00:39.252 --> 00:00:44.860
logs and attacker speculation can expose sensitive information and mislead

9
00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:50.467
leaders. In practice: separate facts, assumptions and unknowns, then record

10
00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:56.075
decisions and the update cadence. Key takeaway: communicate uncertainty clearly;

11
00:00:56.075 --> 00:01:00.000
do not promise what evidence cannot support.

